# Light and Dark Theme Rule

- Treat dual-theme support as a default requirement for all UI and visual design work.
- Use semantic tokens (e.g. theme variables, `bg-surface`, `text-text`, `border-secondary`) instead of hard-coded light-only colors when the design system provides them.
- Ensure contrast and readability in both themes; avoid colors that only work on light or only on dark backgrounds.
- Verify interactive states (hover, focus, disabled) in both themes.
- When adding or updating components, check appearance in light mode and dark mode.
